  <h2>Basic Information</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">Built in 1917 during the Japanese governance period, Taichung Second Market was formerly known as "Shinfucho Market." Centered around a unique hexagonal building with corridors radiating outward, it is one of Taiwan's most historically significant traditional market structures.</p>
  <p>Beyond its rich architectural heritage, the market houses dozens of legendary food stalls passed down through generations. From traditional breakfasts to braised pork rice and retro black tea, it is a must-visit cultural and culinary landmark for all visitors to Taichung.</p>
